SUMMARY:A Taste of Piedmont
LOCATION:Café Q
DESCRIPTION:Category: Food & Beverage\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: Avai
 lable\nTime: 5 PM – 9 PM\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/ev
 ents/209097\n\nLet your palate wander to Northern Italy with our “Taste 
 of Piedmont” dinner specials\, celebrating the rich\, earthy flavors of 
 this renowned culinary region.\n\nAvailable exclusively during dinner serv
 ice\, this limited-time menu showcases the elegance of Piedmont’s season
 al bounty—from silky polenta infused with truffle and black trumpet mush
 rooms to tender braised pork cheeks in Barolo wine\, and delicate porcini-
 studded ravioli. Each dish is designed to highlight the region’s signatu
 re balance of rustic depth and refined technique. Pair with a Barolo or a 
 crisp local white to fully savor the essence of Piedmont.\n\nMake a Reserv
 ation.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/209097
CATEGORIES:Food & Beverage
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-208346@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261103T173000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261103T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261103T210000
SUMMARY:Día de los Muertos: A Taste of Oaxaca
LOCATION:Lunasol
DESCRIPTION:Category: Food & Beverage\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: Avai
 lable\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/208346\n\nIn cel
 ebration of Día de los Muertos\, Lunasol invites members to experience an
  Oaxacan-inspired dinner led by Chef Federico Remberg Roma. For one evenin
 g\, Chef Federico will present a five-course menu that explores the region
 ’s rich culinary heritage through layers of smoke\, spice\, and thoughtf
 ul origin cuisine.\n\nThe evening opens with refined interpretations of Oa
 xacan tradition before progressing to delicately balanced seafood and Wagy
 u beef accompanied by mole negro. Cacao and passion fruit bring the experi
 ence to a vibrant close\, while optional beverage pairings complement each
  stage of the menu. Members are invited to gather in the spirit of Día de
  los Muertos—to share a meal\, honor those we remember\, and celebrate t
 he connections that endure. \n\nMake a Reservation.\n\n*This five-course
  prix fixe menu is offered at $90 per person. Beverages\, taxes & club fee
 s are not included. Dining cancellations less than 48 hours in advance of 
 service\, or failure to attend\, are subject to a 100% charger per member/
 guest. Regular guest policies are in effect.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/208346
CATEGORIES:Food & Beverage
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-208957@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261105T110000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261105T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261105T120000
SUMMARY:Art Tour: Alexandre Gallery Exhibition
LOCATION:Meet in The Lobby
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nStatus: Waitlist Only\nEvent U
 RL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/208957\n\nPlease join 'Quin Ho
 use art curator\, Kate Chertavian for a tour of the 'Quin's Fall exhibitio
 n in collaboration with Alexandre Gallery featuring two generations of fem
 ale New England artists.\n\nThe exhibition showcases ten works by influent
 ial plein air painter\, Lois Dodd\, a key figure in New York's post-war ar
 t scene\, celebrated for her depictions of the Maine landscape. Alongside 
 Dodd's work\, the exhibition highlights paintings by her artistic peers Lo
 ren MacIver and Pat Adams\, as well as contemporary New England artists\, 
 Tessa Greene O'Brien\, Lisa Sanditz and Emily Nelligan.\n\n*This event is 
 complimentary and reserved for members only.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/208957
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-208337@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261106T130000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261106T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261106T160000
SUMMARY:Hands on Impact: Greater Boston Food Bank 
LOCATION:The Greater Boston Food Bank\, South Bay Avenue\, Boston\, MA\, US
 A
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Impact Fund\nPrice: Free\nStatus: Waitlist On
 ly\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/208337\n\nJoin The 
 ’Quin Impact Fund for a hands-on volunteer experience at the Greater Bos
 ton Food Bank\, where members can make a tangible difference in the fight 
 against hunger across our community. Participants will help sort\, package
 \, and organize food donations that support thousands of neighbors in need
  throughout Greater Boston.\n\nThe Greater Boston Food Bank (GBFB)\, New E
 ngland’s largest hunger-relief organization and a member of Feeding Amer
 ica\, distributed 107 million pounds of nutritious food last year alone. T
 hrough the dedication of its staff\, volunteers\, and partners\, GBFB work
 s to provide three meals a day to every person in need in Eastern Massachu
 setts\, supporting healthy lives and thriving communities.\n\n*This event 
 is complimentary and reserved for members only. Please wear comfortable cl
 othing suitable for service and close-toed shoes.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/208337
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Impact Fund
END:VEVENT
