BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-208799@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261110T173000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261110T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261110T190000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: The Success Paradox 
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nStatus: Waitlist Only\nEve
 nt URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/208799\n\n5:30PM Reception
 \, 6:00PM Discussion\nWhat happens when the success you have worked toward
  brings unexpected questions rather than fulfillment? Join psychiatrist an
 d author Dr. Blaise Aguirre for a keynote lecture exploring the emotional 
 complexities of ambition\, achievement\, and what comes next.\n\nDrawing o
 n research for his forthcoming book\, Dr. Aguirre will examine the imposte
 r phenomenon - the feeling that we have not earned our accomplishments - a
 nd the arrival fallacy\, the belief that reaching a goal will deliver last
 ing happiness. From “Do I deserve to be here?” to “How do I sustain 
 this?” and “What now?”\, he will explore the questions that can emer
 ge when high achievers reach the milestones they once imagined would be en
 ough.\n\nWith more than two decades of experience in mental health and as 
 founding medical director of 3East at McLean Hospital\, Dr. Aguirre brings
  a compassionate perspective to the pursuit of success. The conversation i
 nvites us to consider how we define achievement - and how greater self-und
 erstanding can help us build a life that feels as meaningful as it looks.\
 n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members only. Complimenta
 ry light bites and refreshments will be served. Cancellations made within 
 24 hours of the event\, or failure to attend\, will result in a $25 charge
 .
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/208799
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-208800@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261110T183000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261110T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261110T200000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: Old in the Game - A Reflection of Hip-Hop History 
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 26 spots left\nS
 tatus: Available\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/20880
 0\n\n6:30PM Reception\, 7:00PM Discussion \nIn celebration of Hip-Hop His
 tory Month\, join author Murray Forman\, Boston hip-hop pioneer Edward “
 Edo.G” Anderson\, and Black music and culture scholar Emmett G. Price II
 I for a conversation about longevity\, identity\, and legacy in hip-hop.\n
 \nDrawing from Forman’s book Old in the Game: Aging In and With Hip-Hop
 \, the discussion will explore how the culture’s pioneering artists and 
 audiences navigate aging\, generational differences\, and the balance betw
 een honoring the past and creating what comes next. Edo.G brings the persp
 ective of a career spanning more than three decades\, from his breakthroug
 h with Ed O.G. and Da Bulldogs to enduring collaborations with Pete Rock a
 nd Masta Ace. Price adds his insight as a musician and scholar whose work 
 examines hip-hop’s cultural influence and the connections between genera
 tions.\n\nTogether\, they will consider what it means to grow older within
  hip-hop - and how the artists who helped define the culture continue to s
 hape its future.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members 
 only. Complimentary light bites and refreshments will be served. Cancellat
 ions made within 24 hours of the event\, or failure to attend\, will resul
 t in a $25 charge.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/208800
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-209103@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261111T163000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261111T163000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261111T180000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: The Instinct of Opportunity with Mellody Hobson 
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nStatus: Waitlist Only\nEve
 nt URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/209103\n\n4:30PM Reception
 \, 5:00PM Discussion\n\nJoin Sandy Edgerley\, Co-Founder of The ’Quin Ho
 use\, and Mellody Hobson\, Co-CEO of Ariel Investments\, for a conversat
 ion about leadership\, investment\, and the instinct to see possibility be
 fore it becomes obvious.\n\nFrom guiding Ariel’s growth to founding Proj
 ect Level®\, Mellody has built a career around ideas with the power to c
 hange industries. Together\, she and Sandy will explore what it takes to t
 urn conviction into action\, with a closer look at the momentum behind wom
 en’s sports. As new audiences\, investment\, and influence reshape the f
 ield\, they will consider who gets to define its future—and what this mo
 ment reveals about opportunity in business.\n\n*This event is complimentar
 y and reserved for members only. Complimentary light bites and refreshment
 s will be served. We kindly ask that all cancellations be made at least 24
  hours prior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/209103
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-210561@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261111T180000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261111T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261111T193000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: Liberation & Legacy - A Veterans Day Conversation
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 120 spots le
 ft\nStatus: futureSale\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events
 /210561\n\n6:00PM Reception\, 6:30PM Discussion \nThis Veterans Day\, joi
 n The ’Quin for a conversation honoring the American soldiers who libera
 ted Nazi concentration camps and the survivors whose lives they helped res
 tore.\n\nModerated by Jody Kipnis\, President and CEO of Holocaust Museum 
 Boston\, the discussion brings together Mike Ross\, son of Holocaust survi
 vor Steve Ross\, who was liberated from Dachau\, and Jim Kelliher\, son of
  an American soldier who helped liberate concentration camps.\n\nDrawing o
 n their fathers’ experiences\, a handwritten letter from May 1945\, and 
 an original booklet documenting the 11th Armored Division\, the panel will
  explore liberation through the intertwined stories of those who survived 
 and those who came to their aid. Guests will also have the opportunity to 
 view Steve Ross’s flag and historical documents on display throughout th
 e evening\, offering a tangible connection to the lives and events at the 
 heart of the conversation.\n\nTogether\, we will reflect on the courage an
 d service we honor on Veterans Day - and our shared responsibility to carr
 y these stories forward.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for 
 members only. Complimentary light bites and refreshments will be served. C
 ancellations made within 24 hours of the event\, or failure to attend\, wi
 ll result in a $25 charge.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/210561
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-209680@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261111T190000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261111T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261111T203000
SUMMARY:Meet the Maker: Tom Gamble of Gamble Estates
DESCRIPTION:Category: Food & Beverage\nPrice: Free\nStatus: Waitlist Only\n
 Event URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/209680\n\nGreat wine be
 gins long before the first pour. Join Tom Gamble\, Founder and Vigneron of
  Gamble Estates\, for an exploration of Napa Valley through the lens of a 
 third-generation farmer. Begin with a welcome glass of 2025 Yountville Sa
 uvignon Blanc before discovering a selection of 2023 reds showcasing Mount
  Veeder\, Rutherford\, and Oakville. Along the way\, Tom will share how r
 egenerative farming\, a century of family roots\, and a collaboration with
  Atelier Melka shape wines that tell the story of their origins.\n\n*This 
 event is complimentary and reserved for members only. Complimentary light
  bites and refreshments will be served. Cancellations made within 24 hour
 s of the event\, or failure to attend\, will result in a $25 charge.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/209680
CATEGORIES:Food & Beverage
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-195306@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261112T180000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261112
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261113
SUMMARY:5th Anniversary 'House Celebration: A Night of Gathering & Impact
LOCATION:Offsite: MGM Music Hall
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Impact Fund\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: 
 Available\nTime: 6 PM – 10 PM\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.c
 om/events/195306\n\nThanks to the incredible enthusiasm from Members wishi
 ng to join the party on November 12th\, please enjoy extended seating opt
 ions at MGM as we turn the venue inside out for an extraordinary night of
  entertainment! Look forward to design inspiration\, nostalgic expressions
 \, and musical programming inspired by The 'Quin\, promising an evening th
 at we'll be talking about for decades... \n\nAs a reminder\, the clubhous
 e will be closed on this afternoon and throughout the evening beginning at
  3PM on November 12th as we prepare to welcome you to our temporary addres
 s at MGM Music Hall for the night. \n\nA schedule of world-class perform
 ances by EGOT-winning\, multi-platinum artist and producer John Legend and
  the Grammy-winning Gipsy Kings featuring Nicolas Reyes\, with net proceed
 s benefiting The ’Quin Impact Fund.\n\n6:00PM | Doors Open\n\n7:15PM |
  Program Begins\n\nwith Opening Act by The Gipsy Kings featuring Nicolas R
 eyes\n\n8:45PM | John Legend\n\nThe stage is set. We're delighted to cel
 ebrate five remarkable years of The ’Quin with you - the leaders\, creat
 ors\, innovators\, and rising stars of our community who are shaping Bosto
 n's legacy.\n\nIf you have not yet secured a seat\, please consider the ex
 tra tickets released today!\n\nEnter the password QUINMEMBER to unlock all
  extended and remaining theater and box seat tickets.\n\nPurchase Theater 
 or Box Seats\nIf you prefer a 'Quin-inspired Residential Seating Arrangeme
 nt on the Ground Floor\, a limited number of cabaret tables (seat 4)\, and
  lounges (seat 8)\, are available on a first-to-reserve basis. These packa
 ges begin at a $2\,000 commitment and include bespoke food and beverage pa
 ckages.\n\nRequest Residential Seating Options\nShould you require assista
 nce or have any related questions please email the dedicated Impact Concie
 rge Team at Impact5More@thequin.com. We look forward to celebrating with y
 ou in November!        \n\n*Ticket prices vary by seating location an
 d package. Tickets are reserved for members\, plus three guests aged 21+. 
 Tickets are limited\, available on a first-to-reserve basis\, and nonrefun
 dable and nontransferable. Please note that The ‘Quin House will close 
 at 3:00PM on this date to ensure access to this celebration for the entire
  ‘Quin House Team.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/195306
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Impact Fund
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-209681@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261113T140000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261113T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261113T153000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: The Art of the City - Why Cultural Philanthropy Matters
  Now
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 24 spots lef
 t\nStatus: Available\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/2
 09681\n\n2:00PM Reception\, 2:30PM Discussion \n\nTo celebrate Town & Co
 untry’s milestone 180th anniversary\, Editor in Chief Stellene Volandes
  and The ‘Quin Co-Founder Sandy Edgerley will host a timely conversation
  on the vital role cultural philanthropy plays in shaping Boston and its f
 uture.\n\nThe Art of the City - Why Cultural Philanthropy Matters Now brin
 gs together an extraordinary group of leaders from across Boston’s cultu
 ral\, civic\, and philanthropic communities to explore the power of the ar
 ts\, the importance of investing in our cultural institutions\, and the fu
 ture of philanthropy for the next generation.\n\nJoining the conversation 
 along with Stellene and Sandy will be Peggy Fogelman\, Norma Jean Calderwo
 od Director of the Isabella Stewart Gardner Museum and Joseph Henry\, Chie
 f\, Mayor’s Office of Arts and Culture\, City of Boston.\n\nThe discussi
 on will be moderated by Adam Rathe\, Senior Features Director at Town & C
 ountry. A Q&A will follow.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved fo
 r members only. Complimentary light bites and refreshments will be served
 . Cancellations made within 24 hours of the event\, or failure to attend\
 , will result in a $25 charge.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/209681
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-208597@thequinhouse.com
