SUMMARY:The Scottie's Sessions: Live Jazz with Northstar
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: Food & Beverage\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: Avai
 lable\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/208597\n\nSlip i
 nto Scottie’s for an evening of live jazz with an unexpected edge as Nor
 th Star takes the stage. Featuring tap\, tenor saxophone\, piano\, and bas
 s\, the quartet brings a playful twist to classic jazz\, with tap joining 
 the ensemble as both movement and percussion.\n\nGrab a cocktail\, settle 
 in\, and let the evening unfold—one beat\, note\, and step at a time.\n\
 nReservations are not required.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/208597
CATEGORIES:Food & Beverage
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-209682@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261113T190000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261113T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261113T203000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: The Second Half of Athleticism - The Athlete's Dilemma
LOCATION:The Muse
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 60 spots lef
 t\nStatus: futureSale\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/
 209682\n\n7:00PM Reception\, 7:30PM Discussion \nWhat happens when organi
 zed competition ends\, but the athlete in us remains? For those who once b
 uilt their lives around practices\, teammates\, and seasons\, stepping awa
 y can raise questions of identity\, purpose\, and how we care for ourselve
 s beyond the demands of competition.\n\nDr. Rich Joseph\, Harvard Medical
  School faculty physician and Founder of VIM Medicine\, returns to The ’
 Quin to launch a three-part series exploring what it means to remain an at
 hlete for life. He will moderate a conversation with Marcus Wilson\, co-fo
 under of NOBULL\; Ben Bergeron\, founder of CompTrain and coach to multipl
 e CrossFit Games champions\; and Jeremy Bettle\, a performance and sports 
 science leader whose work spans professional sports and who now leads Vita
 lity Collective.\n\nTogether\, they will explore how we redefine ambition\
 , find new sources of motivation\, and build a lasting relationship with m
 ovement. It’s a candid look at life after the final whistle—and how th
 e discipline\, resilience\, and sense of possibility that shaped us as com
 petitors can continue to serve us for decades to come.\n\n*This event is c
 omplimentary and reserved for members only. Complimentary light bites and 
 refreshments will be served. Cancellations made within 24 hours of the eve
 nt\, or failure to attend\, will result in a $25 charge.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/209682
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
