BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-210562@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261116T180000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261116T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261116T193000
SUMMARY:Author Talk: "The Greatest Adventurer" with Geoffrey Kent and Ben M
 ezrich 
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 100 spots left\n
 Status: futureSale\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/210
 562\n\n6:00PM Reception\, 6:30PM Discussion \nFrom a single Land Rover in
  the African bush to the global travel company Abercrombie & Kent\, Geoffr
 ey Kent has built a life around taking the road less traveled. Join The �
 �Quin for a conversation with the explorer and entrepreneur\, moderated by
  co-author of The Greatest Adventurer\, Ben Mezrich\, on the adventures\,
  ambitions\, and personal stakes behind an extraordinary career.\n\nDrawin
 g on his memoir\, The Greatest Adventurer: From the Wilds of Africa to a 
 Billion-Dollar Travel Empire\, Kent will share stories from a lifetime of 
 exploration—from crossing Africa alone by motorbike at sixteen to naviga
 ting the Amazon and pioneering a new era of luxury travel. Guided by the p
 hilosophy “Shoot with a camera\, not with a gun\,” his work has helped
  shape the relationship between travel and conservation.\n\nBeyond the exp
 editions lies an equally compelling story of entrepreneurship and family: 
 the risks of building a global business\, the relationships tested along t
 he way\, and the complicated question of what we leave behind. Together\, 
 Kent and Mezrich will explore the instinct to venture further—and what i
 t takes to know when you have arrived.\n\n*This event is complimentary and
  reserved for members only. Complimentary light bites and refreshments wil
 l be served. Cancellations made within 24 hours of the event\, or failure 
 to attend\, will result in a $25 charge.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/210562
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
