BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-209702@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261117T130000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261117T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261117T150000
SUMMARY:90 Minutes of Innovation
LOCATION:The Pub
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 150 spots le
 ft\nStatus: futureSale\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events
 /209702\n\n1:00PM Program\, 2:30PM Networking\nWhat happens when artificia
 l intelligence steps off the screen and into the physical world? Join The 
 ’Quin for an afternoon exploring how robotics is changing the way we mov
 e\, work\, and interact with technology - and what it takes to bring those
  advances into everyday life.\n\nJohn Werner - venture capitalist\, active
  member of the MIT community\, and Forbes AI columnist - will lead a conve
 rsation with Conor Walsh\, Harvard’s Paul A. Maeder Professor of Enginee
 ring and Applied Sciences and founder of the Harvard Biodesign Lab\, and T
 om Ryden\, Executive Director of MassRobotics.\n\nWalsh’s work in soft r
 obotics and wearable exosuits is helping people regain mobility and perfor
 m physically demanding tasks with less strain. At MassRobotics\, Ryden con
 nects entrepreneurs\, researchers\, investors\, and industry to help emerg
 ing robotics companies grow. Together\, they offer complementary perspecti
 ves on the journey from a promising prototype to a technology that improve
 s people’s lives.\n\nThe evening will also mark five years of innovation
  programming at The ’Quin\, with Werner sharing highlights from more tha
 n 50 programs that have brought members into conversation with the people 
 shaping our future. From the inaugural TEDxBoston in 2021 to today’s exp
 lorations of robotics and physical AI\, curiosity remains at the heart of 
 it all.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members only. Com
 plimentary light bites and refreshments will be served. Cancellations made
  within 24 hours of the event\, or failure to attend\, will result in a $2
 5 charge.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/209702
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
